{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Glutton.</b> It is explicit, and it is 'a glutton of meat' (Proverbs 23:20), only it is a general term for one who gives himself over to everything he desires, everything he craves." "<b>And drunkard.</b> One who drinks much, and he is one who gets drunk. Now this is like an Epicurean, for he does not seek the life of this world except to indulge in every kind of food and drink. And this section is juxtaposed because of the beautiful woman, and the witness, and 'his mother's name.' And the hint that I hinted at concerning the sons of Aaron."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:14.596195592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}